	<item>
		<title><![CDATA[Bob and Pat Hoos]]></title>
		<link>https://allsaintsconcord.org/bob-and-pat-hoos/</link>
		<pubDate>Mon, 24 Nov 2025 18:51:55 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[BrianSapp-Moore]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://allsaintsconcord.org/?p=17500</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4 class="wp-block-heading">White Oak (Cornus Alba)</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Given by Kim Everhardt in loving memory of her parents.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Bob and Pat Hoos loved the outdoors and found joy in spending time in nature. Their ashes rest in the mountains of Appalachia. This white oak is a perfect place to visit and reflect on the cherished memories their family shared.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>To learn more about this tree, go to <a href="https://plants.ces.ncsu.edu/plants/quercus-alba/">https://plants.ces.ncsu.edu/plants/quercus-alba/</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->]]></content:encoded>
		<excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[]]></excerpt:encoded>
